### A. a submodule working tree, with a worktree added beside it

The submodule's .git is a link into the superproject's Git directory:
  …/app/parser/.git: gitdir: ../.git/modules/parser

so the worktree listing names that Git directory where a checkout is expected:
  worktree /tmp/stepstone-r3/work/app/.git/modules/parser
  HEAD da2e2584ab538c9fc36db27e8888efd156fa1222
  branch refs/heads/main
  

The submodule is its repository's one main checkout, so it writes its roadmap:

…/app/parser $ stepstone project add Ship the parser rewrite
Added project goal ship-the-parser-rewrite: Ship the parser rewrite
[exit 0]

An agent then takes a worktree of the submodule to work on a goal:

…/parser-agent $ stepstone project list
[open] ship-the-parser-rewrite: Ship the parser rewrite
[exit 0]

