### C. git init --separate-git-dir that records nothing

Git writes the link from the checkout to the Git directory and nothing back,
so this layout has a main checkout that cannot be named from the Git directory.
The write is still refused - it would fork the roadmap like any other - and the
refusal says what is true rather than inventing a path.

…/silent $ stepstone project add Canonical goal
Added project goal canonical-goal: Canonical goal
[exit 0]

…/silent.git $ git config core.worktree   (in the Git directory)
  (unset)

…/silent-agent $ stepstone project add Forked in a worktree --json
